Summary:                    No reported errors, just no sound
Description: 
Apologies in advance if this already has been covered...

Using Debian's standard ALSA configuration tools, the hardware is located
and supposedly configured, but no sound actually comes out through either
the built-in speakers or through the headphone jack.  alsamixer allows me
to enable/disable and control volumes, and aplay, xmms, mpg123, and zinf
with the ALSA plugin all seem to be doing something (ie, the program
appears to play the file for the correct amount of time) but no sound is
emitted.

I've tried adding "snd-atiixp" and "snd-atiixp-modem" to /etc/modules,
I've tried commenting out, I've tried having an "alsa-base" file in
/etc/modutils and in /etc/modprobe.d (latter generated by Debian's
alsaconf util)

Any suggestions would be GREATLY appreciated...
